A standard traversal uses a current pointer initialized to head. A while loop continues as long as current is not None. Inside the loop, you can process current.data, then advance current = current.next. This pattern works for any singly linked list. Here is a complete example:

```python
class Node:
    def __init__(self, data):
        self.data = data
        self.next = None

class LinkedList:
    def __init__(self):
        self.head = None

    def traverse(self):
        current = self.head
        while current is not None:
            print(current.data)
            current = current.next
```

The loop stops when current becomes None, which marks the end of the list.

